course: dictionary
lesson: 9074
title: Context clues: slob
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are informal, which means people use them in everyday talk, not in formal writing. «Slob» is one of these. Its meaning is a person who is lazy, messy and does not care about being tidy. The sentence around it gives the clue: «Don't be such a slob — pick up your socks!» Socks on the floor show what a slob is like.
explain: Slob is also an insult. Families often say it jokingly, but it can still hurt, so think about how the speaker says it. The dash and the words «pick up your socks» show the speaker is telling someone off. Ask yourself: is this word kind or unkind?
explain: Slob can also be a verb phrase, «slob out» or «slob about» (UK informal). «Slobbing out on the sofa» does not mean being a slob in the rude sense. It means relaxing lazily and doing very little, like lying around all afternoon. The word «sofa» is your clue that it describes doing nothing much.
fact: «Slob» is an informal, rude word for a person who is lazy, messy and does not care about being tidy.
fact: «Slob out» or «slob about» (UK informal) means to relax lazily and do nothing much.
fact: Calling someone a slob is an insult, although families often say it jokingly.
fact: «Svynya» means pig in another language; calling someone «svynya» is an insult meaning a pig or slob.
exercise: «Don't be such a slob — pick up your socks!» What does slob mean here? | A person who is very tidy | *A person who is lazy and messy | A type of sock | A famous chef
exercise: Maya says, «Let's slob out on the sofa this afternoon.» What does slob out mean? | To clean the whole house from top to bottom | *To relax lazily and do very little | To run very fast in a race | To shout loudly at a friend
exercise: Why is «slob» an insult? | It is the name of a famous artist | It means someone is very happy | *It calls someone lazy and messy, which is unkind | It is a number used in maths
test: In a story, a character leaves pizza boxes and dirty clothes everywhere. What kind of character is this? | *A slob | A bird that sings | A tidy, neat character | A friendly robot
test: «Svynya» means pig, and calling someone «svynya» is an insult. What does the context tell you about how it is used? | It means someone is clean | *It is an insult | It is the name of a town | It is a polite greeting
exam: Which sentence best shows someone slobbing out? | Cooking a big dinner for the whole family | Running a race across the park | *Lying on the sofa all afternoon, doing nothing much | Scrubbing the bathroom until it shines
